**Read:** [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), heat/mass-transfer coupling and evaporation; [CoolProp — thermophysical property models and methods](../sources/CoolProp-Thermophysical-Property-Methods.lingua#r_2QYM459W81KPNJK37RHJ6VB9R1), humid-air definitions, equations and domain; [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1), mixture activities and equilibrium.

Distinguish relative humidity, humidity ratio, water activity, dew point and wet-bulb conditions. Specify total pressure and the mixture model. Relative humidity alone does not determine the water mass carried by a stream.

Couple evaporation/condensation with energy and mass balances, including latent energy and changing gas/liquid composition. In drying, internal transport and material binding can control the rate after an externally controlled stage. Shrinkage, porous structure and temperature history may change properties and quality.

Construct a complete air/water state and balance example with a verified property model. Compare an idealized psychrometric process with a documented dryer or enclosure case. The thermal foundation supports later agriculture, buildings and process engineering without silently treating their biological or material constraints as solved.

